```
node_modules

dist/
# The Android project carries real customisation — the OAuth intent filter, the signing config,
# the manifest placeholders — and `tauri android init` regenerates it from a template. Ignoring the
# whole directory meant those edits lived on one machine only, so a CI-built APK silently lacked the
# deep-link filter that makes a browser sign-in able to come back. Track the sources; ignore the
# build outputs, the caches, and the native libraries cargo produces.
src-tauri/gen/apple/
src-tauri/gen/schemas/
src-tauri/gen/android/**/build/
src-tauri/gen/android/.gradle/
src-tauri/gen/android/local.properties
src-tauri/gen/android/**/jniLibs/
src-tauri/gen/android/app/keystore.properties
src-tauri/gen/android/app/tauri.properties

# large mongod sidecar binaries (kept on disk, bundled at build time)
binaries/mongod-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
src-tauri/binaries/mongod-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
